WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.737
On the Flight and Arrival.

2
00:00:02.017 --> 00:00:06.390
Day 29 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.164
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.444 --> 00:00:18.767
Today's goal: talk to cabin crew and passengers, handle seat problems and connections, and get through immigration, baggage and customs on arrival.

5
00:00:19.047 --> 00:00:21.287
(See Airport for check-in and security.).

6
00:00:22.637 --> 00:00:23.490
Part 1.

7
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:24.730
Key words.

8
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.324
Here is a quick table:

9
00:00:27.604 --> 00:00:43.241
Word or phrase, and Meaning. cabin crew or flight attendant: staff on the plane. overhead bin or locker: storage above seats. aisle or window or middle seat: seat positions. seat belt sign: light that says: stay seated,

10
00:00:43.521 --> 00:00:56.471
belt on. turbulence: bumpy air. connecting flight or connection: your next flight. transit or transfer desk: help desk for connections. landing card or arrival form: form for immigration.

11
00:00:57.821 --> 00:01:05.927
baggage claim or carousel or belt: where bags arrive. customs or declare: check of goods or tell officials what you're carrying.

12
00:01:07.277 --> 00:01:08.152
Part 2.

13
00:01:08.432 --> 00:01:10.245
Questions you'll ask (on board).

14
00:01:11.495 --> 00:01:13.522
Excuse me, I think you're in my seat.

15
00:01:13.802 --> 00:01:15.061
I'm in 14C.

16
00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.751
Could you help me put my bag in the overhead bin?

17
00:01:18.031 --> 00:01:19.738
Is it possible to change seats?

18
00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:22.087
There's an empty one in row 20.

19
00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:25.717
Could I have some water or a blanket or a vegetarian meal?

20
00:01:25.997 --> 00:01:28.087
What time do we land, local time?

21
00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:29.861
Will I make my connection?

22
00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:31.655
I only have 50 minutes.

23
00:01:31.935 --> 00:01:34.367
Which gate does my connecting flight leave from?

24
00:01:35.717 --> 00:01:38.661
Do I need to collect my bag before my connecting flight?

25
00:01:40.011 --> 00:01:40.907
Part 3.

26
00:01:41.187 --> 00:01:42.553
Questions you'll be asked.

27
00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.147
Here is a quick table:

28
00:01:45.427 --> 00:01:47.645
Crew or officer asks, and You answer.

29
00:01:47.925 --> 00:01:49.547
Chicken or vegetarian?:

30
00:01:49.827 --> 00:01:51.256
Vegetarian, please.

31
00:01:51.536 --> 00:01:52.709
Something to drink?:

32
00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:56.147
Just water, please. / Tea with milk, no sugar.

33
00:01:56.427 --> 00:01:59.243
Could you put your seat upright or open the window shade?:

34
00:01:59.523 --> 00:02:00.547
Sure, sorry.

35
00:02:00.827 --> 00:02:02.064
Purpose of your visit?

36
00:02:02.344 --> 00:02:03.368
(immigration):

37
00:02:03.648 --> 00:02:04.459
Business.

38
00:02:04.739 --> 00:02:06.979
I'm attending a meeting at our office here.

39
00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:08.645
How long are you staying?:

40
00:02:08.925 --> 00:02:09.949
Six days.

41
00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.893
I fly back on the 18th.

42
00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:13.411
Anything to declare?

43
00:02:13.691 --> 00:02:14.565
(customs):

44
00:02:14.845 --> 00:02:18.451
No, nothing. / Yes, I have some sweets for my family.

45
00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:20.718
Part 4.

46
00:02:20.998 --> 00:02:22.918
Conversation 1: on board.

47
00:02:24.168 --> 00:02:26.195
Here is how the conversation goes.

48
00:02:26.475 --> 00:02:29.269
Excuse me, I think you're sitting in my seat.

49
00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.555
I'm in 22A, the window.

50
00:02:31.835 --> 00:02:32.880
Oh, sorry!

51
00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:34.867
I thought this was 21.

52
00:02:35.147 --> 00:02:36.235
Let me move.

53
00:02:36.515 --> 00:02:37.709
No problem.

54
00:02:37.989 --> 00:02:38.928
Thank you.

55
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:40.211
Good evening.

56
00:02:40.491 --> 00:02:43.008
Could you put your bag under the seat in front, please?

57
00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:44.568
The bins are full.

58
00:02:44.848 --> 00:02:45.573
Sure.

59
00:02:45.853 --> 00:02:47.731
Could I have a blanket, please?

60
00:02:48.011 --> 00:02:49.376
It's a bit cold.

61
00:02:50.726 --> 00:02:52.326
The conversation continues.

62
00:02:52.606 --> 00:02:54.121
Of course, I'll bring one.

63
00:02:54.401 --> 00:02:55.211
Thanks.

64
00:02:55.491 --> 00:02:58.158
And do you know what time we land in Singapore?

65
00:02:58.438 --> 00:03:00.230
At 6:40 local time.

66
00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.281
That's about 20 minutes early.

67
00:03:02.561 --> 00:03:03.307
Great.

68
00:03:03.587 --> 00:03:05.827
I have a connecting flight to Sydney.

69
00:03:06.107 --> 00:03:08.134
Do I need to collect my bag?

70
00:03:09.484 --> 00:03:11.084
The conversation continues.

71
00:03:11.364 --> 00:03:13.135
If it's on the same ticket, no.

72
00:03:13.415 --> 00:03:14.631
It's checked through.

73
00:03:14.911 --> 00:03:16.809
The transfer desk can confirm.

74
00:03:17.089 --> 00:03:18.455
Thank you very much.

75
00:03:19.805 --> 00:03:20.765
Part 5.

76
00:03:21.045 --> 00:03:23.839
Conversation 2: immigration on arrival.

77
00:03:25.089 --> 00:03:27.116
Here is how the conversation goes.

78
00:03:27.396 --> 00:03:28.804
Good morning.

79
00:03:29.084 --> 00:03:30.364
Passport, please.

80
00:03:30.644 --> 00:03:31.732
Good morning.

81
00:03:32.012 --> 00:03:33.164
Here you are.

82
00:03:33.444 --> 00:03:35.151
What's the purpose of your visit?

83
00:03:35.431 --> 00:03:36.284
Business.

84
00:03:36.564 --> 00:03:39.487
I'm attending a training at our Sydney office.

85
00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:41.153
How long will you stay?

86
00:03:42.503 --> 00:03:44.103
The conversation continues.

87
00:03:44.383 --> 00:03:45.471
Seven days.

88
00:03:45.751 --> 00:03:48.482
My return flight is on the 22nd.

89
00:03:48.762 --> 00:03:49.999
Where are you staying?

90
00:03:50.279 --> 00:03:51.965
At the Harbour View Hotel.

91
00:03:52.245 --> 00:03:53.439
Here's the booking.

92
00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:55.917
Is this your first visit to Australia?

93
00:03:56.197 --> 00:03:57.327
Yes, it is.

94
00:03:58.677 --> 00:04:00.277
The conversation continues.

95
00:04:00.557 --> 00:04:02.029
Are you carrying any food?

96
00:04:02.309 --> 00:04:03.973
Yes, some packaged snacks.

97
00:04:04.253 --> 00:04:06.237
I've declared them on the form.

98
00:04:06.517 --> 00:04:07.627
Okay.

99
00:04:07.907 --> 00:04:09.187
Enjoy your stay.

100
00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:10.405
Thank you.

101
00:04:11.755 --> 00:04:12.694
Part 6.

102
00:04:12.974 --> 00:04:14.147
When things go wrong.

103
00:04:15.397 --> 00:04:18.213
My flight was delayed and I've missed my connection.

104
00:04:18.493 --> 00:04:19.539
Can you rebook me?

105
00:04:19.819 --> 00:04:21.291
My bag hasn't arrived.

106
00:04:21.571 --> 00:04:23.021
Here's my baggage tag.

107
00:04:23.301 --> 00:04:24.517
Where do I report it?

108
00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.400
My bag is damaged: the handle is broken.

109
00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.173
I'd like to file a report.

110
00:04:29.453 --> 00:04:30.499
I feel unwell.

111
00:04:30.779 --> 00:04:32.080
Could I have some water?

112
00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.088
Do you have anything for nausea?

113
00:04:34.368 --> 00:04:36.523
Sorry, I didn't understand the question.

114
00:04:36.803 --> 00:04:38.211
Could you repeat it, please?

115
00:04:39.561 --> 00:04:40.499
Part 7.

116
00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:41.697
Practice.

117
00:04:42.947 --> 00:04:49.624
Answer the immigration officer in one clear sentence each: purpose, length of stay, where you're staying, your job.

118
00:04:50.974 --> 00:04:51.891
Success:

119
00:04:52.171 --> 00:04:53.323
Sample answers.

120
00:04:53.603 --> 00:04:54.947
I'm here on holiday.

121
00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:56.273
For ten days.

122
00:04:56.553 --> 00:04:59.198
At my sister's house in Melbourne; here's the address.

123
00:04:59.478 --> 00:05:00.865
I'm a software engineer.

124
00:05:02.215 --> 00:05:03.089
Part 8.

125
00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:04.415
Speak today.

126
00:05:05.665 --> 00:05:10.230
Practise the immigration answers out loud until you can say them without stopping.

127
00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:14.905
Learn 3 on-board requests by heart: water, blanket, help with a bag.

128
00:05:16.255 --> 00:05:17.791
That's the end of this lesson.

129
00:05:18.071 --> 00:05:22.721
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

130
00:05:23.001 --> 00:05:29.124
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

